<v Robyn Semien>我很好，谢谢。

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:03.370
<v Lisa Estrada>Good. I know, I saw--
<v Lisa Estrada>很好。我知道，我看到——

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:13.720
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>20 years after she left the team, Robyn called her old coach to say, I'm talking about you on the radio as my protector. Do you think about yourself that way?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她离开球队20年后，Robyn给她的老教练打电话说，我在广播里提到你是我作为保护者。你认为自己是那样的人吗？

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:26.890
<v Lisa Estrada>Yeah, I mean, if people need to say that I'm, you know, mama hen, or I act like a mom, then I'm totally fine with that. And I think that I should be here to protect them.
<v Lisa Estrada>是的，我的意思是，如果人们需要说我是个“老母鸡”，或者我的行为像个妈妈，那我完全没问题。而且我认为我应该在这里保护她们。

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:46.630
<v Lisa Estrada>Sometimes it's a bit hard coming into a sports world with them. Sports world is a man's world, kind of. And there's definitely the stigma of they're just eye candy. And they go out, and they shake their pom-poms. Or they go out, and they dance, or whatever it is.
<v Lisa Estrada>有时带着她们进入体育界有点困难。体育界是男人的世界，某种程度上。而且绝对有“她们只是花瓶”的污名。她们出去，她们摇动绒球。或者她们出去，她们跳舞，或者不管是什么。

00:23:46.630 --> 00:23:55.620
<v Lisa Estrada>But I wanted everyone in Los Angeles to understand they're not only dancing girls, they are so much more than that. And they should be looked at as professional women.
<v Lisa Estrada>但我希望洛杉矶的每个人都明白，她们不仅仅是舞蹈女孩，她们远不止于此。她们应该被视为职业女性。

00:23:55.620 --> 00:24:20.790
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Lisa says she doesn't remember calling water bottles porny. But she's sure if she did, it was only because she wanted the women to be seen as professional. And Robyn says it worked. Yes, having a rule to tell you how often to change your tampon is ridiculous. But taken as a group, these rules made the whole thing into a job. They did make everything feel professional.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Lisa说她不记得把水瓶称为色情。但她肯定如果她这么说了，那只是因为她想让这些女性被视为专业人士。Robyn说这很有效。是的，有关于多久换一次卫生棉条的规则是荒谬的。但作为一个整体来看，这些规则把整件事变成了一份工作。它们确实让一切感觉很专业。

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:39.840
<v Robyn Semien>There is something wholesome about going to an NBA basketball game. There's families and kids. And it's bright. And it's familiar. And yes, and we were like the dance team that was wearing the logo that was printed on the outside of this massive stadium.
<v Robyn Semien>去现场看一场NBA篮球比赛有一种健康的感觉。有家庭和孩子。它是明亮的，是熟悉的。是的，我们就像是印在这个巨大体育场外面的带有标志的舞蹈队。

00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:56.470
<v Robyn Semien>It just felt like, OK, we're all in it. Like we all kind of know what it is. And maybe we're like the sexualized talent entertainment component to all this, but it feels very rated G.
