<v Robyn Semien>他只是那样对我们说。你会想，为什么你不说“说茄子”呢？然后你就会记得。你会想，但实际上，我站在那儿，穿着聚拢文胸，穿着和我在海滩上差不多的衣服，在一个有成千上万穿得比我多得多的观众的体育场里。你会有这种感觉的瞬间：哦。

00:25:54.900 --> 00:26:07.320
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And there was the time they did the event at a bar called Pinky's. It was a pool hall where all the tables were covered in pink felt. The Laker Girls did their routines, but it was late and the men were drunk.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>还有那次她们在一家叫Pinky's的酒吧参加活动。那是一个台球厅，所有的桌子都铺着粉红色的绒布。湖人女孩跳了她们的例行舞蹈，但时间很晚，男人们喝醉了。

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:35.380
<v Robyn Semien>Suddenly, you're, like, doing dance routines in like a smoky pool hall packed with kind of screaming men. And I feel like I had a-- like, something switched for me. Like, I saw what I was doing in a different way. It was just like one of those times where I thought, this feels like stripping right now.
<v Robyn Semien>突然，你在那种烟雾缭绕的台球厅里跳舞，周围挤满了尖叫的男人。我觉得我有种感觉——就像对我来说有什么东西切换了。就像我以一种不同的方式看待我所做的事情。那只是那种我以为这感觉就像脱衣舞的时候之一。

00:26:35.380 --> 00:26:49.610
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But then the event at Pinky's was over. And Robyn says those awkward moments usually faded quickly, because she loved the job. She loved what she was doing. And that, I guess, is what was still confusing to me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但Pinky's的活动结束后。Robyn说那些尴尬的时刻通常很快就消失了，因为她热爱这份工作。她热爱她所做的一切。我想，这就是我仍然感到困惑的地方。

00:26:49.610 --> 00:27:02.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What is to love? You've got a coach who's up in your business, all of your business. You don't make a lot of money-- although in Robyn's case, the NBA pays a lot better than the NFL. But still, it's not player money.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>有什么可爱的？你有一个干涉你私事的老板，干涉你所有的私事。你赚不到很多钱——尽管在Robyn的情况下，NBA的薪水比NFL好得多。但仍然，那不是球员的钱。

00:27:02.770 --> 00:27:27.950
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You can't gain three pounds. You can't even talk to the attractive famous young men right next to you. You can't drink bottled water. The more I learned, the more cheerleading sounds like walking through airport security over and over every day, just the feeling of being heavily policed with a bunch of unexplained arbitrary rules that are maybe there to keep you safe, but you don't really get why.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你不能胖三磅。你甚至不能和你旁边有吸引力的著名年轻男性说话。你不能喝瓶装水。我了解得越多，啦啦队听起来就越像每天一遍又一遍地通过机场安检，那种被严密监管的感觉，带着一堆无法解释的任意规则，也许它们是为了保证你的安全，但你真的不知道为什么。

00:27:27.950 --> 00:27:37.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And just, isn't it supposed to be fun? Is it fun? Robyn looks at me kind of pityingly when I ask about this.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>而且，这难道不应该很有趣吗？它有趣吗？当我问这个问题时，Robyn带着同情的眼光看着我。

00:27:37.260 --> 00:27:38.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is it fun?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>它有趣吗？

00:27:38.460 --> 00:28:03.680
<v Robyn Semien>I don't know that I can compare anything to being on stage in front of-- like, in a stadium under those lights in front of, like, 25,000 screaming fans. Even when I think about it now, it doesn't exactly feel like me. It's a little out-of-body.
<v Robyn Semien>我不知道我能把任何事情和站在25,000名尖叫粉丝面前的体育场舞台灯光下相比。即使我现在想到它，它也不太像我。有点出窍的感觉。

00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:05.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In like an awesome way?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>以一种棒极了的方式？

00:28:05.250 --> 00:28:15.310
<v Robyn Semien>In an amazing way, yeah. In an amazing way.
<v Robyn Semien>以一种惊人的方式，是的。以一种惊人的方式。

