00:30:13.590 --> 00:30:30.550
<v Nancy Updike>Employee Christmas parties are so often associated with bad behavior and just unwise choices that I believe they rival wedding toasts. About three years ago, Robert Faturechi, a reporter for the LA Times , heard about a Christmas party thrown by the Los Angeles County Sheriff's Department.
<v Nancy Updike>员工圣诞派对通常与不良行为和不明智的选择联系在一起，以至于我相信它们可以与婚礼祝酒词相媲美。大约三年前，《洛杉矶时报》的记者Robert Faturechi听说洛杉矶县治安官部门举办了一场圣诞派对。

00:30:30.550 --> 00:30:36.740
<v Robert Faturechi>At this beautiful banquet hall, there had been a massive fight between deputies.
<v Robert Faturechi>在这个美丽的宴会厅里，副警长之间发生了一场大规模的斗殴。

00:30:36.740 --> 00:30:55.750
<v Nancy Updike>This fight was not an argument. It was a fistfight among sheriff's deputies. And in Los Angeles County, sheriff's deputies are guards in the county jails, which does not mean that they're watching a few drunks sleep it off in a holding cell. This is the largest jail system in the country-- over 19,000 inmates at the moment.
<v Nancy Updike>这场斗殴不是争论。这是副警长之间的拳头斗殴。而在洛杉矶县，副警长是县监狱的守卫，这并不意味着他们是在监视几个醉汉在拘留室里睡觉。这是全国最大的监狱系统——目前有超过19,000名囚犯。

00:30:55.750 --> 00:31:13.110
<v Nancy Updike>So Robert heard about the deputies' brawl at the Christmas party. And he started looking into what had happened. What he heard was that one group of deputies had beat up two other deputies. And the deputies who delivered the beating all worked on the same floor in the Sheriff Department's main jail.
<v Nancy Updike>所以Robert听说了副警长在圣诞派对上的打架事件。他开始调查发生了什么。他听说一群副警长殴打了另外两名副警长。而那些动手殴打的副警长都在治安官部门主要监狱的同一层工作。

00:31:13.110 --> 00:31:30.280
<v Robert Faturechi>It's called the 3000 floor. And I heard word that before the fight broke out, when they were exchanging words, these guys were throwing three-finger hand signs, similar to gang signs. There were rumors that they described themselves as the 3000 boys.
<v Robert Faturechi>它被称为3000层。我听说在打架爆发前，当他们交换言语时，这些人正在比划三指手势，类似于帮派手势。有传言说他们称自己为“3000男孩”。

00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:30.780
<v Nancy Updike>Mhm.
<v Nancy Updike>嗯。

