00:32:04.980 --> 00:32:44.640
<v Nancy Updike>Robert dug into public records about use of force reports in the jail, and later, internal Sheriff's Department documents-- these had never been made public-- that showed that the department knew that brutality against inmates was a real problem in the jails, that deputies were beating inmates, fabricating stories to justify beatings, that investigations after the fact were shoddy. Robert was also hearing more and more from sources inside the Sheriff's Department. He published a series of stories with headlines like, "LA County Deputy Says He Was Forced to Beat Mentally Ill Inmate" and "Monitor Says She Saw Deputies Beat Inmate, quote, 'Like a Punching Bag.'"
<v Nancy Updike>Robert深入挖掘了关于监狱使用武力报告的公共记录，以及后来——从未公开过的——内部治安官部门文件，这些文件显示，部门知道针对囚犯的暴行是监狱里的一个真正问题，副警长正在殴打囚犯，编造故事来为殴打辩护，事后的调查也是敷衍了事。Robert还从治安官部门内部的线人那里听到了越来越多的消息。他发表了一系列文章，标题如《洛杉矶县副警长称他被迫殴打精神病囚犯》和《监督员称她看到副警长殴打囚犯，“就像打沙袋一样”。》

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:51.760
<v Nancy Updike>Robert talked to a former commander who said there were deputies who really did seem to have formed their own gangs in the jail.
