00:32:51.760 --> 00:33:16.000
<v Robert Faturechi>I mean, this was a high-ranking guy. He told us that deputies were literally breaking inmates' bones. In order to get membership into these gang-like groups of deputies, they had to break inmates' bones. And, I mean, that's the kind of thing that if I had heard before all of this started to unfold, I would never believe it.
<v Robert Faturechi>我的意思是，这是一个高级别的人。他告诉我们副警长确实在折断囚犯的骨头。为了获得这些副警长帮派组织的成员资格，他们必须折断囚犯的骨头。而且，我的意思是，如果我在这一切开始展开之前听说过这种事，我永远不会相信。

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:28.550
<v Robert Faturechi>But this was a department commander telling us this. I mean, this guy was in charge of hundreds of deputies. He's someone who came up through the system who has a lot of loyalty to the system.
<v Robert Faturechi>但这是一位部门指挥官告诉我们的。我的意思是，这家伙负责数百名副警长。他是通过系统晋升起来的，对系统有很强的忠诚度。

