<v Nancy Updike>治安官部门说是的，他们打断了FBI与Brown的会面，但这是根据一项新加强的安全协议来保护他。事实上，他们说所发生的一切都不是蓄意的妨碍司法。他们说他们把Anthony Brown在监狱里转来转去并藏起来不是为了让他远离联邦政府，而是为了让他免受他所举报的副警长可能的报复。

00:52:36.700 --> 00:52:58.110
<v Nancy Updike>So far, jurors have not bought these arguments. Toward the end of 2013, the Feds brought obstruction of justice cases against seven people in the LA County Sheriff's Department. Six have been convicted, including the two sergeants who went to FBI Agent Leah Marx's home. One more case ended with a hung jury. It's going to be retried.
<v Nancy Updike>到目前为止，陪审员们并没有相信这些论点。在2013年底，联邦政府对洛杉矶县治安官部门的七个人提起了妨碍司法诉讼。六人被定罪，包括那两名去FBI探员Leah Marx家的中士。另一个案件以陪审团僵局结束。它将被重审。

00:52:58.110 --> 00:53:38.020
<v Nancy Updike>But Robert, the LA Times reporter, said even before these convictions, even before anyone was charged in these obstruction cases, the Sheriff's Department was coming under more pressure than it ever had to deal with brutality against inmates by deputies. The FBI investigation came on top of a whole pile of complaints and evidence that had been building up for years, from civilian monitors of the police, from the ACLU, from media reports. Facing all that, the sheriff implemented reforms. And now, Robert says from everything he hears from people on the inside, though there's still problems in the jails, the inmates are treated differently.
<v Nancy Updike>但Robert，《洛杉矶时报》的记者说，甚至在这些定罪之前，甚至在妨碍司法案件中任何人被指控之前，治安官部门正受到比以往任何时候都更大的压力，去处理副警长针对囚犯的暴行。FBI的调查是在多年来积累的一整堆投诉和证据之上进行的，来自警察的民间监督员，来自美国公民自由联盟（ACLU），来自媒体报道。面对所有这些，治安官实施了改革。而现在，Robert说从他从内部人士那里听到的所有事情来看，尽管监狱里仍然存在问题，但囚犯的待遇有所不同。

00:53:38.020 --> 00:54:16.430
<v Nancy Updike>A few months ago, Sheriff Lee Baca, who had headed the department for 15 years, resigned. One last fact to chew on-- the Sheriff's Department plan to hide Anthony Brown in the jail system was called Operation Pandora's Box. I didn't quite do a double take when I read that, but I did think it wasn't the best myth to choose. The story doesn't end well for anyone who's hoping to contain something or keep it hidden. Pandora opens the box, and the contents fly out for the whole world to see.
<v Nancy Updike>几个月前，领导该部门15年的治安官Lee Baca辞职了。最后一个值得思考的事实——治安官部门在监狱系统里藏匿Anthony Brown的计划被称为“潘多拉魔盒行动”。我读到那个时并没有感到惊讶，但我确实认为这不是选择的最佳神话。对于任何希望控制某些东西或保持其隐藏的人来说，这个故事的结果并不好。潘多拉打开了盒子，里面的东西飞出来让全世界都看到了。

00:54:16.430 --> 00:54:30.200
<v Ira Glass>Nancy Updike is one of the producers of our program. Robert Faturechi is a reporter at the Los Angeles Times who's covered law enforcement since 2010. We contacted the LA County Sheriff's Department about the recent history of violence against inmates in the jails. And they sent this statement.
<v Ira Glass>Nancy Updike是我们节目的制片人之一。Robert Faturechi是《洛杉矶时报》的记者，自2010年以来一直报道执法工作。我们就监狱中针对囚犯的暴力行为的近期历史联系了洛杉矶县治安官部门。他们发来了这份声明。

00:54:30.200 --> 00:55:04.240
<v Ira Glass>Quote, "Over the past few years, the department has made a multitude of changes which have transformed the custody environment. Some of these changes include innovative ideas which have not previously been implemented in large jail systems. Use of force incidents have dropped significantly in comparison to 2011 and earlier."
<v Ira Glass>引用，“在过去几年里，该部门进行了大量的改革，改变了羁押环境。其中一些改革包括在大型监狱系统中以前从未实施过的创新想法。与2011年及以前相比，使用武力事件显著下降。”

00:55:04.240 --> 00:55:23.800
<v Ira Glass>Well, our program was produced today by Miki Meek with Alex Blumberg, Ben Calhoun, Sean Cole, Stephanie Foo, Chana Joffe-Walt, Sarah Koenig, Jonathan Menjivar, Brian Reed, Robyn Semien, Alissa Shipp, and Nancy Updike. Our senior producer is Julie Snyder. Production help from Alison Davis and JP Dukes. It is Alison's last program with us here as our visiting fellow, and we all wish her the best.
<v Ira Glass>嗯，我们的节目今天由Miki Meek制作，Alex Blumberg，Ben Calhoun，Sean Cole，Stephanie Foo，Chana Joffe-Walt，Sarah Koenig，Jonathan Menjivar，Brian Reed，Robyn Semien，Alissa Shipp和Nancy Updike参与。我们的资深制片人是Julie Snyder。制作帮助来自Alison Davis和JP Dukes。这是Alison作为我们访问学者在我们这里的最后一个节目，我们祝她一切顺利。

